From 4561ba95e439ee595b29f748a4081fb6776fc3a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reto Gantenbein <reto.gantenbein@linuxmonk.ch>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:54:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] incusd: Set httpmuxgo121=0 GODEBUG default

incusd moved from gorilla/mux to http.ServeMux, which relies on the
wildcard pattern syntax added in Go 1.22 ("/{$}", "/1.0/operations/{id}/wait"
and so on).

That syntax is gated behind the httpmuxgo121 GODEBUG setting. Builds with a
main module take the modern default from the go directive in go.mod, but
builds without one -- GOPATH mode, which is what Fedora's %gobuild macro
still uses -- fall back to the pre-1.22 defaults, where httpmuxgo121=1
selects the Go 1.21 muxer. Every wildcard route then fails to match, so the
daemon answers 404 for most of its API. Cluster bootstrap fails on
/1.0/operations/{id}/wait and the guestapi socket 404s on /, which shows up
as three failures in cmd/incusd's own tests.

cmd/incus-agent already carries this directive for exactly this reason; do
the same for incusd.

Signed-off-by: Reto Gantenbein <reto.gantenbein@linuxmonk.ch>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cmd/incusd/main.go | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cmd/incusd/main.go b/cmd/incusd/main.go
index 9fab6b3be..825995b86 100644
--- a/cmd/incusd/main.go
+++ b/cmd/incusd/main.go
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+//go:debug httpmuxgo121=0
+
 package main
 
 import (
